<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Txfio</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Txfio</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <VersionPrefix>0.2.0</VersionPrefix>
    <PackageId>Txfio</PackageId>
    <Authors>YUKIKEDA</Authors>
    <Description>Transactional file IO for Windows (NTFS/SMB), inspired by git staging and commit.</Description>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 YUKIKEDA and contributors</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/YUKIKEDA/Txfio</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/YUKIKEDA/Txfio.git</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
    <PackageTags>filesystem;transaction;windows;ntfs;smb</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
0.2.0 has breaking changes. A crashed transaction no longer blocks the whole work folder, and the names of staging entries are reserved.

- The static entry class Txfio is now TxFileIO (TxFileIO.BeginAsync, TxFileIO.RecoverAsync), so the calls compile after `using Txfio;`.
- Do not share a work folder between 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 clients.
- RecoveryRequiredException comes from staging and CommitAsync for overlapping paths only, not from BeginAsync. RecoverAsync runs while other transactions are alive and reports RecoverResult.Contended.
- CreateDirectoryAsync reserves its directory until the transaction ends.
- Paths with a staging name ({name}.{txid}.txnew, .txnew.prev, .txold) throw InvalidOperationException. Listings and copies skip every transaction's staging entries. New: TxFileIO.IsStagingName.
- A directory DeleteAsync conflict names the blocking child in ExternalConflictException.Path.

Full notes and how to move: https://github.com/YUKIKEDA/Txfio/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0" PrivateAssets="All" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Txfio.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
